# GMS raises Elemental Drain's rate TO 5% a burn over the same count of five,
# so a full count is worth 25% rather than 15%. It supersedes rather than adds:
# one rate, the better of the two, exactly as Advanced Blessing supersedes
# Bless.
#
# What that makes it is a bossing passive, which is what GMS calls it: on a map
# the count is at its cap whatever the character does, and on a boss it is
# however many burns the rotation is keeping on the one enemy.
#
# It opens just above the 3% a maxed Elemental Drain pays and climbs to GMS's
# 5%, the shape every superseding skill here takes -- Advanced Blessing starts
# where Bless left off for the same reason.
#
# It does not pass its master level. GMS masters this at 1 and does not mark it
# for Combat Orders, so there is no level above the top for a grant to reach.
name: "Fervent Drain"
description: "Increases the effect of Elemental Drain."
kind: SKILL_KIND_PASSIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_FIRE_POISON_ARCH_MAGE skill_order: 10 }
max_level: 10
supersedes_skill_name: "Elemental Drain"
dot_count_cap: 5
base { final_dmg_pct_per_dot: 0.032 }
per_level { final_dmg_pct_per_dot: 0.002 }
